# Non-circular gear pair, driven through the packaged FreeCAD 1.1.3.
#
#   reprocad record ~/dev/freecad.noncirculargears/tests/noncircular-gears.steps \
#       --binary /usr/bin/freecad --profile noncircular
#
# The profile is a saved home whose Mod directory links to this workbench, so
# the run loads it the way an installed addon is loaded.
#
# Three things are on screen rather than asserted: the pair appears meshed at
# one click, the dialog that opens over it rebuilds both gears as it is filled
# in, and editing f(x) in the property editor afterwards rebuilds them again -
# the second gear is derived from the first, so it has to follow.
#
# Axonometric is a submenu, not a view: stopping on it leaves the whole View
# menu open over the tree, and every step after it aims at a covered screen.
#
# The dialog's own steps are left to search the whole screen. It is a floating
# Tasks panel in this profile and a docked one in others, so a region around
# where it happens to sit is a region that only holds in one of them.
#
# Return inside the dialog presses its default button and takes the whole thing
# with it, so its fields are left with Tab. The property editor's fields want
# the opposite: Return is what commits an edit there.

note step 1 - a new document
menu File > New Document for:40
sleep 6

note step 2 - switch to the Non-Circular Gear workbench
menu View > Workbench > Non-Circular Gear for:40
sleep 8

note step 3 - one command builds both gears and opens them for setting up
menu Non-Circular Gear > Gear Pair for:40
sleep 10
menu View > Standard views > Axonometric > Isometric for:40
sleep 3
menu View > Standard views > Fit all for:40
sleep 5

note step 4 - every row of the dialog is a property of the gear itself
waittext mate turns for:40
sleep 8

note step 5 - a mate that turns twice needs an f(x) that repeats twice
field function for:40
sleep 2
key ctrl+a
type 1 + 0.45 * cos(2 * x)
key Tab
sleep 10
field mate turns for:40
sleep 2
key ctrl+a
type 2
key Tab
sleep 12
menu View > Standard views > Fit all for:40
sleep 6

note step 6 - OK keeps the pair the dialog was filled in for
clickon OK for:40
sleep 8

note step 7 - what the pair came out at, the mate's own tooth count included
clickon NonCircularGear in:0,150,420,90 for:40
sleep 5
scroll 200 800 -8
sleep 2
waittext mate teeth in:0,520,420,420 for:40
sleep 8

note step 8 - a different f(x), typed in place, and both gears rebuild
scroll 200 800 8
sleep 2
field function in:0,520,420,420 for:40
sleep 2
key ctrl+a
type 1 + 0.45 * cos(4 * x)
key Return
sleep 12
menu View > Standard views > Fit all for:40
sleep 8

note step 9 - from above, both gears rebuilt and still meshed
menu View > Standard views > Top for:40
sleep 4
move 700 900
sleep 8
